From 47c55e03f983e00610ae13890b146e53dfad605f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:34:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/24] Re-read IOSurface page lists without a vCPU through a
 validated walk

Since the drain moved to a worker thread, a type-11 mapping's page list
is never re-read where the writes happen: read_kva needs a vCPU, answers
NoCpu there, and resolve keeps whatever page list the last vCPU resolve
adopted. A surface the guest re-wired keeps being written at its old
pages, and pages that were unwired at that resolve stay holes for good
(13.6's black wallpaper: holes=4093 of=9216, every write-back refused).

Capture the EL1 translation state (TTBR1, TCR, SCTLR) on the vCPU when
the guest publishes on the mapper ring, through read_xreg indices from
0x1000 that a matching QEMU change answers, and walk kernel addresses in
software over guest physical memory from the worker with a small ARM64
stage-1 walker of its own. It refuses what it does not implement: the
MMU off, big-endian, TTBR1 walks disabled, 64 KiB granules, 52-bit
addresses, blocks where the granule allows none.

The walk serves a thread without a vCPU only after runtime validation:
every kernel read on a vCPU is read again through the walk and compared,
and a root needs eight agreeing non-zero reads over three pages, one of
them across a page boundary, and no disagreement. A changed root or a
device reset starts validation again; a disagreement retires the root.

REIMS_VGPU_KVA_WALK picks what happens without a validated root.
strict, the default, refuses the re-read: the page list is withdrawn and
the write fails and is reported lost, never written through the cache,
and each refusal is logged with the mapping and its time. compat keeps
the cached page list as before, for a QEMU without the shim change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 87aad01f515940d36564dde8c190eb7a25127653)
